{"repositoryId":1334394558,"availability":"available","full":"Quincunx33/phishGard","name":"phishGard","description":"Defensive server-side phishing URL analysis with headless auditing and Gemini supplemental intelligence","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":8,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-14T16:54:46Z","updated":"2026-08-14T16:55:18Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://phishguard-7buolmv8.manus.space","topics":["cybersecurity","gemini","headless-browser","phishing-detection","react","threat-detection","typescript","url-analysis"],"demo":"https://phishguard-7buolmv8.manus.space/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:43.074Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:43.074Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:43.074Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T18:04:43.074Z","stars":8,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Know before you click. A defensive, server-side URL intelligence tool that audits suspicious links, explains the evidence behind a risk score, and keeps the browser away from the target site.","PhishGuard is designed for safe, explainable phishing triage. The submitted URL is sent to the PhishGuard server; the user's browser does not contact the target. The server performs bounded checks, renders pages in an isolated headless Chromium context, and combines deterministic evidence with an optional Gemini supplemental assessment.","PhishGuard is not a credential tester, crawler, or exploitation tool. It does not submit forms, transmit browser credentials, download target files, or allow arbitrary browser-to-target communication. Redirects, private addresses, popups, downloads, and browser lifecycle failures are bounded and sanitized."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Quincunx33/phishGard/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d8301ca14a4ea6e871961d08eeed004f39746b7d160c0673dbdca3d9efcd281e","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T18:04:43.220Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15